# LoRa Gateway & Transmitter Walkthrough

I have implemented a dual-hardware system for your "Smart Waste Management" project using the **NodeMCU ESP8266**, **HC-SR04**, and **RYLR998 LoRa transceivers**.

## Hardware Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Bin Node 1 (Transmitter)"
        T1["HC-SR04"] --> N1["NodeMCU"]
        N1 --> L1["RYLR998"]
    end
    subgraph "Bin Node 2 (Transmitter)"
        T2["HC-SR04"] --> N2["NodeMCU"]
        N2 --> L2["RYLR998"]
    end
    L1 -. "LoRa" .-> LGR["Gateway Node (Receiver)"]
    L2 -. "LoRa" .-> LGR
    LGR --> NG["NodeMCU"]
    NG -- "WiFi" --> AWS["AWS Backend"]
```

## 1. Bin Transmitter Setup

The [lora_transmitter.ino](file:///c:/Users/DELL/OneDrive/Desktop/smart-waste-management/hardware/bin_sensor/lora_transmitter.ino) file handles the sensor measurement and LoRa transmission.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Deep Sleep Connection**: You MUST connect a wire between **RST** and **D0** on the NodeMCU. Without this, the board will not wake up from sleep!
> 
> **Wiring Checklist**:
> - HC-SR04 VCC -> 5V Boost
> - HC-SR04 Echo -> D6 (NodeMCU) via Voltage Divider
> - RYLR998 TX -> D1 (NodeMCU)
> - RYLR998 RX -> D2 (NodeMCU)

## 2. Gateway Receiver Setup

The [lora_gateway.ino](file:///c:/Users/DELL/OneDrive/Desktop/smart-waste-management/hardware/bin_sensor/lora_gateway.ino) file listens for data from all bins and forwards it to your live AWS server.

> [!WARNING]
> **Gateway Power**: The Gateway cannot use Deep Sleep. It must stay connected to a power source to receive reports from the bins at any time.
>
> **WiFi Config**: Update the `ssid` and `password` in the code if your network changes.

## 3. Communication Protocol

The bins send a lightweight comma-separated string to minimize air-time:
`[BIN_ID],[FILL_LEVEL],[STATUS]`
Example: `BIN-001,85,Full`

## Performance Tips

1.  **Baud Rate**: If you see garbage characters in the Serial Monitor for LoRa, use `AT+IPR=9600` on the RYLR998 modules to lower the baud rate for more reliable `SoftwareSerial` performance.
2.  **Antenna**: Ensure the brass coil antenna is soldered securely for maximum range (up to several KM line-of-sight).
